; The expression-grade coverage instrumenter. Reachable as a dune
; instrumentation backend under two names, and the difference between
; them is load-bearing:
;
; - `--instrument-with ppx_windtrap` resolves the (instrumentation.backend)
;   field on the ppx_windtrap library. That library's OTHER job is the
;   inline-test rewriter, so it carries
;   (ppx_runtime_libraries ppx_windtrap.runtime ppx_windtrap.config) — and
;   dune adds a rewriter's ppx_runtime_libraries to everything it
;   preprocesses, instrumentation included. An instrumented library
;   therefore links the windtrap CORE, not just the coverage runtime.
;
; - `--instrument-with ppx_windtrap.coverage` resolves the field below,
;   on the rewriter itself, whose only runtime library is
;   windtrap.coverage. That is the form this file's last paragraph
;   promises, and the only one a library UNDER the core can use: adding
;   the first spelling to lib/dune is a dependency cycle
;   (windtrap -> ppx_windtrap.runtime -> ppx_windtrap -> windtrap), which
;   is how the difference was found.
;
; ppx_windtrap.mutate settles the same question the same way and its dune
; file argues the self-naming pattern at length: dune resolves
; --instrument-with <name> by reading the (instrumentation.backend) field
; of the library called <name>, and does not object to that field naming
; the library that carries it.
;
; Both spellings stay: the first is what the manual documents and what
; every published example uses, the second is what keeps the core out of
; an instrumented library's closure. Prefer the second in new code.
;
; The rewriter is also usable directly with
; (preprocess (pps ppx_windtrap.coverage)), which the semantics tests
; rely on. ppx_runtime_libraries makes every instrumented library link
; the windtrap.coverage runtime the generated code calls - and nothing
; else: instrumented user code must never pull the windtrap core into its
; closure.

(library
 (name windtrap_coverage_ppx)
 (public_name ppx_windtrap.coverage)
 (kind ppx_rewriter)
 (libraries ppxlib windtrap_ppx_scaffold)
 (ppx_runtime_libraries windtrap.coverage)
 (instrumentation.backend
  (ppx ppx_windtrap.coverage))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppxlib.metaquot)))
